From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH kbase-common 017] panvk: hide unvalidated extensions

Do not expose depth-clamp-zero-one, pipeline-binary, or robustness2 until
their advertised behavior has direct workload coverage on the target.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ panvk_per_arch(get_device_extensions)(const struct panvk_physical_device *device)
-      .KHR_depth_clamp_zero_one = true,
+      .KHR_depth_clamp_zero_one = false,
@@ -89,12 +89,12 @@ panvk_per_arch(get_device_extensions)(const struct panvk_physical_device *device)
-      .KHR_pipeline_binary = true,
+      .KHR_pipeline_binary = false,
@@
-      .KHR_robustness2 = PAN_ARCH >= 10,
+      .KHR_robustness2 = false,
